    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n79554" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάρημαι</span></b> , used as pf.
		
			Pass.
		 of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρίζω</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be seated beside</i> or
			<i>by</i>, c. dat., only part., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηυσὶ παρήμενος</span>
			<i>seated by</i> . . , <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.421
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				488
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δηοῦς ἐσχάραις παρημένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					290
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλοτρίοισι π</span>. <i>seated
				at</i> another man's table, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				17.456
			</span></i> : generally, <i>dwell beside</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύεσσι π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				13.407
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> abs., <i>sit
				by</i> or <i>near</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρήμενοι ἄλλοθεν ἄλλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.311
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				19.209
			</span></i> ; of the vultures of Tityos, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑκάτερθε παρημένω ἧπαρ ἔκειρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.578
				</span></i>
			.</div>
